  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently on the Open-Beta, if you create any new avatar for testing. It won't show up until the game is restarted. Forcing me to either 'Build & Test' before launching the game, or restarting the game everytime I wish to test a new avatar.\nThe issue happens the opposite as well, if I delete any local-testing avatars while the game is open, the 'Others' section in the avatar menu still shows the entry of the deleted avatar.\nHow to reproduce:\n1. Launch VRChat and wait until VRChat is completely loaded\n2. Press \"Build & Test\" in the SDK (or) Delete any existing \"Build & Test\" avatars\nWhat should happen (like in the public build): The entries in the 'Others' section of the avatar menu is updated accordingly\nWhat actually happens in Open-Beta: Nothing changes\nP.S. in the SDK \"Offline Testing\" is inaccurate because you need to log-on into the game to test avatars, please switch it so it matches world local testing",
